# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform.
#
# build.sh is Render's build command and runs on Linux. A CRLF checkout makes
# the kernel read the shebang as "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and the deploy fails
# with `env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` -- a confusing error that
# says nothing about line endings, on a file that looks correct in every
# editor. core.autocrlf is a per-clone setting, so it cannot be relied on.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the files a container or Render runs directly.
Procfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
